### Mock payment providers (Lab 2) – called by the REST Connectors
### "Charge payment – primary provider" and "Charge payment – backup provider".
### Mock tokens only: never send real card numbers or credentials.

### 1. Primary provider: approved charge
POST http://localhost:8082/mock/payment-gateway/primary/charges
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": "ORD-API-1", "amount": 215.76, "currency": "EUR", "paymentToken": "tok_test_approve", "customerReference": "CUST-0001"}

### 2. Primary provider: declined charge (HTTP 200, status DECLINED – a business answer, not an error)
POST http://localhost:8082/mock/payment-gateway/primary/charges
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": "ORD-API-2", "amount": 553.79, "currency": "EUR", "paymentToken": "tok_test_decline_funds", "customerReference": "CUST-0004"}

### 3. Backup provider: approved charge
POST http://localhost:8082/mock/payment-gateway/backup/charges
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": "ORD-API-3", "amount": 409.79, "currency": "EUR", "paymentToken": "tok_test_approve", "customerReference": "CUST-0001"}

### 4. Break / repair a dependency (fault injection). Known faults:
###    primary-payment-down  -> primary provider HTTP 503 -> process falls back to the backup provider
###    backup-payment-down   -> backup provider HTTP 503  -> retries -> incident
###    inventory-service-down -> inventory worker fails   -> retries -> incident
###    primary-carrier-down  -> BPMN error CARRIER_UNAVAILABLE -> backup carrier
POST http://localhost:8082/admin/faults/primary-payment-down?enabled=true

###
POST http://localhost:8082/admin/faults/primary-payment-down?enabled=false

### 5. Current fault switches
GET http://localhost:8082/admin/faults

### 6. Start an order instance via the Camunda REST API
POST http://localhost:8080/v2/process-instances
Content-Type: application/json

{"processDefinitionId": "order-fulfilment", "variables": {"orderId": "ORD-HTTP-1", "customerReference": "CUST-0001", "productId": "PRD-1001", "quantity": 2, "deliveryPreference": "STANDARD", "paymentToken": "tok_test_approve"}}

### 7. Customer sends a new payment method after a decline (correlates to the waiting instance by orderId)
POST http://localhost:8080/v2/messages/publication
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "payment-method-updated", "correlationKey": "ORD-HTTP-1", "variables": {"paymentToken": "tok_test_approve"}}

### 8. Evaluate the priority decision directly
POST http://localhost:8080/v2/decision-definitions/evaluation
Content-Type: application/json

{"decisionDefinitionId": "order-priority", "variables": {"deliveryPreference": "EXPRESS", "customerCategory": "VIP", "orderTotal": 300}}
